  "body": "Tucked away at the end of a long driveway in a wonderfully private and peaceful setting, 24 John Dee Crescent is a home with a delightful surprise in store. From the moment you step inside, an expansive open-plan living space welcomes you with an incredible sense of light, space and elevated views across the beautifully landscaped gardens, with a distant view of the sea in the background.  Lovingly refurbished and transformed by the current owners, this is a home they wish they could take with them, but with work calling them to a new city, it's time for their next adventure and an opportunity for a new family to fall in love with everything it has to offer.\r\n\r\nBuilt in low-maintenance brick and block, this beautifully updated home combines modern comforts with relaxed family living and effortless entertaining, where the outdoors beckon and everyone has room to find their own space.\r\nHere are six reasons we think you'll fall in love:\r\n\r\nExpansive open-plan living, dining and kitchen create a stunning first impression, thoughtfully reconfigured with walls removed to maximise light, space and flow, while capturing elevated views over the private backyard and out towards the coast\r\n\r\nA stunning designer kitchen is the star of the show, featuring gorgeous pendant lighting, quality new appliances and an oversized stone island with breakfast bar. Flowing seamlessly onto an entertaining deck with pergola, it's the perfect setting for casual family meals, weekend BBQs and long summer afternoons with friends\r\n\r\nBeautifully landscaped, easy-care tiered backyard offers a private and peaceful haven with plenty of room to kick a ball, add a trampoline or perhaps create your own spa pool retreat\r\n\r\nFour bedrooms and two bathrooms are conveniently located on the main living level, while downstairs a cleverly reconfigured open landing with direct garden access offers a flexible space for a home office, reading nook, sitting area or second lounge\r\n\r\nTucked away downstairs, the generous master suite has been thoughtfully created as a private parents' retreat, complete with an impressive walk-through wardrobe and a beautifully renovated tiled ensuite bathroom\r\n\r\nExtensive improvements throughout include fresh interior and exterior paint, new carpet, laminate flooring in the kitchen and living areas, new curtains and blinds, updated bathroom fittings and a new entrance bannister. The upgraded 1.5-car garage features a new door, carpeted floor, plywood-lined walls and a dedicated laundry area\r\n\r\nPerfectly positioned in Red Beach, you'll enjoy the best of coastal living with everyday convenience close at hand. Spend your weekends swimming at Red Beach, exploring the beautiful estuary walkways or enjoying the cafes, restaurants and golden sands of nearby Orewa. Families will appreciate the proximity to local schools, parks and playgrounds, while Silverdale's shopping centre, supermarkets and motorway access make commuting and everyday living easy.\r\n\r\nAuction: 4:00pm, Thursday 5 November 2026, In Rooms, Ray White Orewa (unless sold prior). You can watch the auction live here https://rwcarpenterrealty.co.nz/watch-our-auctions-live",
